# Typographical conventions (editorial pass)

When editing manuscript Markdown under `when-others-look-to-you/v1/`, treat **typographical conventions** as part of any **editorial pass** (see `v1/docs/drafting-process.md` Step 5).

- **Authority:** `v1/front-matter/typographical-conventions.md` (what readers see); `v1/docs/book-rules.md` (full rules).
- **Sentence discipline:** prefer short, direct sentences; break up long running sentences for clarity (**Sentence Discipline** and **Editorial pass: complicated sentences** in `book-rules.md`; Step 5 in `drafting-process.md`).
- **Mechanical verification:** run the script in `v1/docs/typography-check.md` after substantive edits.
- **Pull quotes:** no `**` inside `Pull Quote Block` divs; no glossary-bold renewal/erosion/vitality/decay inside pull quotes when structurally meant (**Chapter-End Pull-Quote Convention** in `book-rules.md`).
- **Pattern blocks:** first line `**Pattern: Title**` only; renewing dynamics stay **positive-only** in the body; no extra bold spans in the body.
- **Vignettes:** `### **Short Title**` stays **outside** `Vignette Block`; scene text inside the block has **no** `**` (move labels and analysis after the closing `:::`).

Do not add drive-by bold for glossary terms where the word is ordinary English; follow **Direction vs state** and circulation/correction/permission rules in `book-rules.md`.
